LAND OF WIND SUPPLY-CHAIN OVERVIEW -- QUARTERMASTER DIVISION

The Hidden Sand sits at the heart of an arid nation; nearly all timber,
foodstuff, and raw ore must be caravanned across open desert. This document
summarizes the standing arrangements sustaining the village.

Water: Drawn from the deep village wells and rationed under the Water Ration
Policy. Caravan water is sealed and escorted; theft is a capital matter.

Timber and hardwood: Contracted from the northern oasis mills for puppet
construction and building repair. Shipments move only by night to avoid heat
loss and bandit sighting.

Metal and steel: Forged in-village where possible; specialty ore for iron-sand
work is procured under Kazekage seal.

Escort doctrine: Every caravan crossing the dunes is assigned a genin-to-chunin
escort. The Daimyo of Wind subsidizes major convoys per the funding agreement.
Losses to sandstorm or raider are reported to the Kazekage Office within one
cycle. Sunagakure endures because the desert is respected, not defied.
